<%# A filter sheet's option tree, held back until the sheet is first opened.

    The What and Where trees are ~360 checkbox rows between them — about half the
    feed page's compressed weight, shipped on every request to render a picker most
    visits never open. So the page ships this frame instead, and
    filter-sheets#open fetches the rows on the first open. Same component in the
    feed and the rule editor, as ever: both render it through the same sheets.

    The src rides in `data-src`, NOT `src`: nothing may fetch it on its own — not
    Turbo's lazy IntersectionObserver (on mobile the sheet is a fixed element parked
    exactly one viewport down, so "is it visible" is a rounding question), and not a
    crawler, which would otherwise have found a fresh faceted URL space to walk.

    THE APPLIED VALUES LIVE INSIDE THE FRAME. The option rows are the form's
    submitted inputs, so a sheet that contributes nothing until it's opened would
    make chip removal (which unchecks one input and re-submits) silently drop every
    other applied value — and Save in the rule editor wipe the rule. Staging them
    here keeps the form complete from the first paint; Turbo replaces the frame's
    children wholesale, so the moment the pre-checked tree lands they're gone, with
    no deduping to do. Should the fetch fail, they're still in the form.

    Locals: field ('what'/'where'), name (the param family, 'g'/'l'), values (the
            applied ones), src (where the rows come from). %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag filter_sheet_frame_id(field), data: { src: src } do %>
  <% values.each do |value| %>
    <input type="checkbox" name="<%= name %>[]" value="<%= value %>" checked hidden>
  <% end %>
  <p class="sheet__loading" aria-live="polite"><%= t('events.filter.loading') %></p>
<% end %>
